    ORDER GRANTING JOINT MOTION FOR A REVISED PROCEDURAL SCHEDULE

          THIS MATTER comes before the Co-Hearing Examiners upon the Joint Motion for a

Revised Procedural Schedule (“Joint Motion”) filed by Commission Utility Division Staff

(“Staff”) and Southwestern Public Service Company (“SPS”) (collectively “Joint Movants”). The

Co-Hearing Examiners, having reviewed the Joint Motion, FIND AND CONCLUDE:

          1.      On March 6, 2026, the Joint Movants filed the Joint Motion requesting that the New

Mexico Public Regulation Commission (“Commission”) issue an order revising the procedural

schedule to: (1) extend existing deadlines by approximately one month; (2) set a deadline for SPS

to file a list of revisions under 17.1.3.19(C) NMAC; and (3) vacate and reset the hearing scheduled

to begin on May 26, 2026 for July 7, 2026. 1

          2.      The Joint Movants noted that on February 27, 2026, New Mexico Large Customer

Group (“NMLCG”) and Louisiana Energy Services, LLC (“LES”) filed a joint motion requesting

that the Commission extend the rate suspension period for an additional three months, until




1
    Joint Motion (March 6, 2026) at 1.
