Order Granting Joint Motion for a Revised Procedural Schedule   Docket No. 25-00079-UT



December 20, 2026, so that SPS’s new rates will take effect after the beginning of the Future Test

Year in accordance with the Future Test Year Rule. 2

           3.       The Joint Movants noted that if the Commission extended the rate suspension

period, then the original reason for scheduling the May 26, 2026, hearing – so that the Commission

could issue a final order by September 20, 2026 – no longer applies, 3 and stated that the parties

would benefit from additional time to complete discovery and prepare direct, and then rebuttal,

testimony. 4

           4.       The Joint Movants also requested the Commission set a deadline for SPS to file a

list of revisions to its revenue requirement under 17.1.3.19(C) NMAC, and asserted that extending

the procedural schedule by approximately one month would allow sufficient time for SPS to

submit its list of revisions and for Staff and Intervenors to evaluate those revisions. 5

           5.       The Joint Movants therefore proposed the following revised procedural schedule: 6

Required Action                      Current Deadline               Proposed Deadline
SPS List of Revisions                None                           March 20, 2026
(17.1.3.19(C) NMAC)
Staff and Intervenor Direct          March 27, 2026                 May 1, 2026
Testimony
Rebuttal Testimony                   April 17, 2026                 May 29, 2026
Evidentiary Hearing Begins           May 26, 2026                   July 7, 2026




