           6.   No Parties opposed the Joint Motion. One party, LES, suggested the scheduling of

a status conference if the Joint Motion is granted. 7

           7.   On March 12, 2026, the Co-Hearing Examiners issued their Order Partially

Granting Joint Motion to Extend Rate Suspension Period, which extended the rate suspension

period for SPS’s Advice Notice No. 341 until November 30, 2026.

           8.   Having reviewed the Joint Motion and considered the proposed revised procedural

dates in light of the extended rate suspension period, the Co-Hearing Examiners find that the Joint

Motion should be granted, with the proposed revised procedural dates adopted.

           9.   The Co-Hearing Examiners also generally seek to foster productive communication

amongst the parties and with the Co-Hearing Examiners, and therefore find that they will

coordinate a status conference on or before March 31, 2026.

IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

           A.   The Joint Motion IS GRANTED.

           B.   The SPS List of Revisions, to comply with Rule 17.1.3.19(C) NMAC, shall be filed

by March 20, 2026.

           C.   Staff and Intervenor Direct Testimony shall be filed by May 1, 2026.

           D.   Rebuttal Testimony shall be filed by May 29, 2026.

           E.   The Evidentiary Hearing date of May 26, 2026, is vacated. The Evidentiary Hearing

shall begin on July 7, 2026, and will continue through July 17, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. MT.

           F.   The Co-Hearing Examiners will coordinate a status conference to occur on or

before March 31, 2026.



